From: hawkff <109485367+hawkff@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 05:24:59 +0000
Subject: Turn off heap profiler reporting

Disable the HeapProfilerReporting feature. With it enabled, the browser
decides at every start, with a probability of 0.25% on the Android stable
channel, to sample heap allocations in the browser and its child processes
and to pass periodic snapshots to the metrics service. This build never
uploads metrics, so that work only cost CPU time and memory. Heap sampling
started from DevTools or by tracing uses its own sessions and does not
depend on this feature.

License: GPL-2.0-or-later - https://spdx.org/licenses/GPL-2.0-or-later.html
---
 components/heap_profiling/in_process/heap_profiler_parameters.cc | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/components/heap_profiling/in_process/heap_profiler_parameters.cc b/components/heap_profiling/in_process/heap_profiler_parameters.cc
--- a/components/heap_profiling/in_process/heap_profiler_parameters.cc
+++ b/components/heap_profiling/in_process/heap_profiler_parameters.cc
@@ -126,6 +126,7 @@ constexpr base::FeatureParam<double> kUtilityHashSetLoadFactor{
 }  // namespace
 
 BASE_FEATURE(kHeapProfilerReporting, base::FEATURE_ENABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+SET_CROMITE_FEATURE_DISABLED(kHeapProfilerReporting);
 BASE_FEATURE(kHeapProfilerChurnReporting, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
 
 const base::FeatureParam<double> kHeapChurnSubsamplingChance{
